content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 7.1 mm/s RMS. Figure 3 is the limit to use: weekly readings on both bearing housings are classified by the highest reading. 7.1 mm/s is exactly the boundary between Zone C (4.5-7.1, 'Restricted - plan maintenance') and Zone D (7.1-11.0, 'Damage likely - stop the pump'). The figure does not say which zone a boundary value belongs to. As a conservative planning decision, not a documented rule, treat the reading as Zone D and stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature is 72 C. The manual's bearing housing limits are: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading is 2 C above normal and below the alarm limit. This applies because bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The 'Leakage at shaft seal' symptom does not apply, so seal replacement is not indicated by this report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear (bearing 6312-C3) is the most likely cause. It appears in the troubleshooting table under both 'High vibration' and 'High bearing temperature', and both symptoms are present at the drive end.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is also listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage. This is listed for high vibration only.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation. This is listed for high vibration; check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing. This is listed for high bearing temperature only, so it is less likely to explain the vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop pump P-103, then isolate and drain it before any mechanical work.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before or at shutdown, if it is safe to do so, record vibration velocity on both bearing housings (drive end and non-drive end). Classify the highest reading against Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check bearing grease quantity for over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and the impeller (330 mm, 5-vane) for wear, imbalance or damage. Check NPSH and suction conditions for cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive end HF3-510 (6310-C3).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened (for example, removal of the back pull-out assembly), fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. Tighten fasteners to Table 5 of the manual; the torque values are not in the evidence provided.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, re-align with a laser tool to parallel 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if the mechanical seal has to be disturbed or replaced: fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450. Tighten the gland nut to 30 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On restart, make sure the Plan 11 seal flush is established and the pump never runs dry. Re-measure vibration on both housings to confirm Zone A/B, and confirm housing temperature is at or below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair with HF3-510 if wear is found)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair with HF3-512)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever the casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump. A reading at the Zone C/D boundary is treated as Zone D, 'Damage likely - stop the pump'.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from the pump discharge is in place before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing alarm is 80 C and trip is 90 C. Monitor the temperature trend until the pump is stopped.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement (only if required): 4.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 torques. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B at a 30 Nm gland torque for HF-300 serials HF3-22000 and above. P-103 is serial HF3-22410, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies. Do not fit HF3-450; use HF3-450B at 30 Nm if the seal is disturbed. The manual and Table 5 apply only to serials below HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Figure 3 does not define whether exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS is Zone C or Zone D. The stop decision is a conservative assumption; confirm with reliability engineering or AquaDyne.",
    "No non-drive-end vibration or temperature reading was reported, but the manual requires classifying the highest reading of both housings.",
    "Table 5 fastener torque values are not included in the evidence provided.",
    "Bearing fit and torque details, grease type and correct grease quantity are not given in the evidence.",
    "The evidence does not say whether bearing replacement requires removing the back pull-out assembly or opening the casing (which would require gasket HF3-120 and lifting equipment).",
    "NPSH available and required values for the filtered-water line are not provided, so cavitation cannot be assessed from the evidence.",
    "The manual Revision D issue date is not stated. The bulletin is treated as governing based on its serial applicability.",
    "It is not stated whether the 6.0 h bearing replacement time includes the post-work laser alignment."
  ]
}
